                  <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_601">Worcester,
                        Worcestershire. Benedictine cathedral priory of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>At end are (1) a copy of a letter from Silvestro Gigli, bishop
                        of Worcester, to the prior of Worcester, 1502, and (2) a note recording that
                        'ego' Th., prior of Worcester, has let out 'clavem sigilli communis de
                        persior' to Robert Stabull at the order of the bishop of Winchester, 2
                        September 1502. The book probably belonged therefore to Thomas Mildenham,
                        prior of Worcester, 1499--1507.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">There is a note, crossed through: 'Dompnus
